window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Constance</b></p> <p>Rewind to earlier that morning.</p> <p>\"Wife?\"</p> <p>\"Yes, his wife, as in till death do us part.\" The woman in front of me waved her bony finger in my face that had a big diamond wedding ring on it.</p> <p>I heard Charley, Kitty, and Simmora ranting over Joshua. They weren't paying me and what I faced any attention.</p> <p>\"Let's step to the back,\" she suggested when she looked behind me at my sister and friends.</p> <p>At this point, there was no reason for me to object. She switched toward the back like a model on the runway. I watched her put her briefcase on the table, then she turned to me.</p> <p>The woman wasn't ugly at all. Japanese descent but with no accent. Her lips were full, her hair was long and brunette, and her skin was milky white. Her eyes were round with a slight slant. I saw the cattiness, sneaky, and scheming ways she had about her. She was too posh, almost like an AI image.</p> <p>\"Let's start over—\"</p> <p>\"We really don't have to. Your name is Meixiu Sato-Yoshida, and you are Kiyoshi Lee Yoshida's wife.\" There was no need for her to keep repeating that. I finally got it and realized this was real...</p> <p>Finding out the man Constance possibly fell in love with was married shattered her entire world.</p> <p>Jackie and Charley ended their relationship before it truly began. Charley decided to remain faithful to her boyfriend Joshua. But when it comes out that he did not give Charley the same loyalty, she has to deal with that.</p> <p>Major, Lee's childhood friend, is back in town and has his eyes on Constance. The timing is perfect for him to mend her broken heart.</p> <p>Bruce and Sook Yoshida are still determined to take control of their sons' lives by any means necessary.</p> <p>Trust is broken, certain people will spiral out of control, trauma wounds will reopen, and so much more in this second installment of A Billionaire's Weakness.</p>"; 
